<% noise = run["noise"] || {} -%>
<h1>Noise filtered</h1>
<p>Control A and control A′ run the same Rails version on the same traffic. Anything that differs between them is noise (random tokens, unfrozen time). Differences between control A and candidate B at those paths are not reported.</p>
<ul class="stats">
  <li class="stat"><span class="stat-value"><%= noise["a_vs_a_prime_differences"].to_i %></span> <span class="stat-label">differences between control A and control A′ (noise observed)</span></li>
  <li class="stat"><span class="stat-value"><%= noise["a_vs_b_differences"].to_i %></span> <span class="stat-label">differences between control A and candidate B</span></li>
  <li class="stat"><span class="stat-value"><%= noise["suppressed"].to_i %></span> <span class="stat-label">of those suppressed as noise</span></li>
</ul>
<h2>Masked paths by route</h2>
<% masked = noise["masked_paths"] || {} -%>
<% if masked.empty? -%>
<p>No paths were masked: control A and control A′ produced identical normalized traces.</p>
<% else -%>
<p>A real upgrade difference at one of these paths would also be hidden; check them if a route matters to you (RISKS R11).</p>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Route</th><th scope="col">Masked paths</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
<% masked.each do |route, paths| -%>
    <tr><td><code><%= h(route) %></code></td><td><ul><% paths.each do |p| %><li><code><%= h(p) %></code></li><% end %></ul></td></tr>
<% end -%>
  </tbody>
</table>
<% end -%>
